#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:7
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "## Listing Records\n"
msgstr "<Heading level={2} id=\"record\">レコード</Heading>"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:16
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<TabGroup defaultValue=\"ts\">\n"
"  <TabList>\n"
"    <Tab value=\"ts\">TypeScript</Tab>\n"
"    <Tab value=\"go\">Go</Tab>\n"
"  </TabList>\n"
"  <TabPanels>\n"
"    <TabPanel value=\"ts\">\n"
"    You can read records from a user's data repository with `client.list()`:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:23
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```tsx\n"
"    const posts = await client.list(app.bsky.feed.post, {\n"
"      limit: 10,\n"
"      repo: 'alex.bsky.team',\n"
"    })\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:28
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    Each Lexicon will have its own parameters; for `app.bsky.feed.post`, you can specify the `repo` (a user's handle or [DID](#did-resolution)) and a `limit` on the number of posts to return. \n"
"    </TabPanel>\n"
"    <TabPanel value=\"go\">\n"
"    You can read posts from a user's data repository with `RepoListRecords()`:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:37
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```go\n"
"    resp, _ := comatproto.RepoListRecords(ctx, client,\n"
"        \"app.bsky.feed.post\",  // lexicon\n"
"        \"\",                    // cursor\n"
"        10,                    // limit\n"
"        \"alex.bsky.team\",      // handle or DID\n"
"        false,                 // reverse\n"
"    )\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:45
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    for _, record := range resp.Records {\n"
"        fmt.Printf(\"Record: %s\\n\", record.Uri)\n"
"    }\n"
"    ```\n"
"    </TabPanel>\n"
"  </TabPanels>\n"
"</TabGroup>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:47
#, no-wrap
msgid "Refer to [`app.bsky.feed.post`](https://docs.bsky.app/docs/api/app-bsky-feed-get-posts) for this complete Lexicon.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:49
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "## Getting Records\n"
msgstr "<Heading level={2} id=\"record\">レコード</Heading>"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:58
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<TabGroup defaultValue=\"ts\">\n"
"  <TabList>\n"
"    <Tab value=\"ts\">TypeScript</Tab>\n"
"    <Tab value=\"go\">Go</Tab>\n"
"  </TabList>\n"
"  <TabPanels>\n"
"    <TabPanel value=\"ts\">\n"
"    You can use `client.get()` to read an individual record by its [`rkey`](/specs/record-key):\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:67
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```tsx\n"
"    const post = await client.get(app.bsky.feed.post, {\n"
"      rkey: '3jxf7z2k3q2',\n"
"    })\n"
"    ```\n"
"    </TabPanel>\n"
"    <TabPanel value=\"go\">\n"
"    You can use `RepoGetRecord()` to read an individual record by its [`rkey`](/specs/record-key):\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:75
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  ```go\n"
"  resp, _ := comatproto.RepoGetRecord(ctx, client, \n"
"      \"\",                    // cid (empty for latest)\n"
"      \"app.bsky.feed.post\",  // lexicon\n"
"      \"alex.bsky.team\",      // handle or DID\n"
"      \"3mbl5xdw4yk2r\",       // rkey\n"
"  )\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:82
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  fmt.Printf(\"URI: %s\\n\", resp.Uri)\n"
"  // resp.Value contains the record data\n"
"  ```\n"
"    </TabPanel>\n"
"  </TabPanels>\n"
"</TabGroup>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:85
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "## DID Resolution\n"
msgstr "<Heading level={2} id=\"handle-resolution\">ハンドル解決</Heading>"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:87
#, no-wrap
msgid "In AT, user data is resolved through [DIDs](/guides/sync#data-repositories), also known as [Decentralized Identifiers](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Decentralized_identifier). Most AT Protocol applications use [`did:plc` DIDs](/guides/the-at-stack#did-plc) when registering user accounts.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:89
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can resolve a known username to a DID using the `com.atproto.identity.resolveHandle` endpoint. This means that you can just visit this address in a browser with a `handle=` arugment to look up your DID:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:93
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```\n"
"https://bsky.social/xrpc/com.atproto.identity.resolveHandle?handle=youraccount.bsky.social\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:99
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```\n"
"{\n"
"did: \"did:plc:3vekukmab2djjeengw2o3wln\"\n"
"}\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:101
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Typescript SDK also provides the DID of the currently-authenticated as `client.did`:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:105
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```tsx\n"
"const your_did = client.did\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:107
#, no-wrap
msgid "## Unauthenticated Reads\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:109
#, no-wrap
msgid "Some API endpoints can be accessed without authentication. You can create an unauthenticated client by passing a public API URL to a new `Client`:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:120
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<TabGroup defaultValue=\"ts\">\n"
"  <TabList>\n"
"    <Tab value=\"ts\">TypeScript</Tab>\n"
"    <Tab value=\"go\">Go</Tab>\n"
"  </TabList>\n"
"  <TabPanels>\n"
"    <TabPanel value=\"ts\">\n"
"    ```tsx\n"
"    import { Client } from '@atproto/lex'\n"
"    import * as app from './lexicons/app.js'\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:123
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    const client = new Client('https://public.api.bsky.app')\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:125 src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:148
#, no-wrap
msgid "    As with an authenticated client, you can `.get()` any public records, like a user's profile:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:129
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```tsx\n"
"    const profile = await client.get(app.bsky.actor.profile)\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:139
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    You can make API calls to any Lexicon using the same SDK client pattern. For more examples, refer to [the SDK documentation](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@atproto/lex).\n"
"    </TabPanel>\n"
"    <TabPanel value=\"go\">\n"
"```go\n"
"import (\n"
"\t\"context\"\n"
"\tappbsky \"github.com/bluesky-social/indigo/api/bsky\"\n"
"\t\"github.com/bluesky-social/indigo/xrpc\"\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:141
#, no-wrap
msgid "ctx := context.Background()\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:146
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"client := &xrpc.Client{\n"
"  Host: \"https://public.api.bsky.app\", // public API endpoint\n"
"}\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:151
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```go\n"
"profile, _ := appbsky.ActorGetProfile(ctx, client, \"alex.bsky.team\")\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:156
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"fmt.Printf(\"Handle: %s\\n\", profile.Handle)\n"
"fmt.Printf(\"Display Name: %s\\n\", *profile.DisplayName)\n"
"fmt.Printf(\"Followers: %d\\n\", *profile.FollowersCount)\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/reading-data/en.mdx:161
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    You can make API calls to any Lexicon using the same SDK client pattern. For more examples, refer to [the Go SDK libraries](https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/bluesky-social/indigo).\n"
"    </TabPanel>\n"
"  </TabPanels>\n"
"</TabGroup>\n"
msgstr ""

